/T (Tendon Insertions and Leverage Points: The effectiveness of a muscle depends critically on where its tendon inserts. A tendon that inserts farther from the joint \(like a long wrench\) has a greater mechanical advantage. This means it can move heavier loads, even if the range of motion is smaller. In the forearm, the arrangement of tendon insertions is optimized to generate tremendous grip strength with relatively little muscular effort.)
